  "honest_limitations": [
    "First-order Hoftyzer-Van Krevelen has no pi-cohesion group: bare aromatic and conjugated rings (benzene, styrene) are assigned delta_h=0 and a low aromatic delta_d, so they are the largest-Ra cases and are reported as a DECLARED BOUNDARY, not hidden. Substituted aromatics (toluene, xylenes, ethylbenzene) recover as alkyl groups add.",
    "the predictor uses the MEASURED molar volume V=M/rho; a fully a-priori vector would chain a group-contribution molar volume (Fedors V is separately validated in the molar-volume/density audit), which this audit references but does not re-derive, to isolate the HvK group-parameter accuracy.",
    "literature Hansen triples themselves carry method scatter of order +-0.5-1 MPa^0.5 between compilations; the graded metric is therefore a per-component RMSE and a vector distance benchmarked to the epoxy R0~8-13 selection radius, not a spuriously precise sub-1% number.",
    "Hansen distances here are between a solvent's a-priori and literature POINTS; a full RED-number solvent-selection decision also needs a resin sphere (delta_d, delta_p, delta_h, R0). No single external DGEBA sphere is hardcoded; the operational KPI is instead the self-contained solvent-to-solvent geometry preservation (nearest replacement / blend-toward-target).",
    "20-solvent single-panel study; broader chemistries (amines, glycol ethers, nitrogen heterocycles) are a natural extension, not claimed here."
  ],
