  "redteam_finding_ester_oxygen_double_count": "RED-TEAM FINDING (this run): the RDKit heavy-atom (C,O,Cl) formula guard added by this audit caught that the shared single-pass oxygen classification used by the already-signed Fedors cohesive-energy audit double-counts an ester's single-bonded oxygen as BOTH a COO_ester and an O_ether when RDKit lists that oxygen before the carbonyl oxygen (e.g. ethyl acetate SMILES 'CCOC(=O)C'). That inflates the ester hydrogen-bonding term by the ether Eh (3000 J/mol), giving delta_h(ethyl acetate)=10.1 vs literature 7.2. This audit CORRECTS it with a two-pass oxygen classifier (carbonyl first, consuming the ester O before the ether pass), which the formula guard enforces (ester O count = 2, not 3). The prior signed Fedors receipt is NOT modified (immutable); this is logged as an honest red-team note. Impact on the Fedors audit is minor (its headline was the SCALAR total delta, dominated by delta_d/cohesive energy, so ester total-delta error stayed ~4%); the correction matters specifically for the ester delta_h / Hansen-vector geometry that THIS audit validates.",
